Implementation Structure Overview (ASP.NET Core MVC):
1. Database Connectivity: Configured via Entity Framework Core in Startup.cs using a Connection String to SQL Server.
2. CRUD Implementation (Example: Course Management):
```csharp
// Admin Controller Action for Creating Content
[HttpPost]
[ValidateAntiForgeryToken]
public async Task<IActionResult> Create([Bind("Id,Title,Content,CategoryId")] Course course)
{
    if (ModelState.IsValid)
    {
        _context.Add(course);
        await _context.SaveChangesAsync();
        return RedirectToAction(nameof(Index));
    }
    return View(course);
}
```
3. Client/Server Processing: Utilizes Razor views for server-side rendering and JavaScript/jQuery for client-side form validation and asynchronous requests.
4. Navigation: Implementation of a shared _Layout.cshtml containing a responsive Navigation Bar using HTML5 <nav> elements.
5. CSS Usage: 
- External: Linked custom stylesheet for site-wide branding.
- Internal: Page-specific styling for the Dashboard dashboard views.
- Inline: Critical element-level overrides for multimedia positioning.
